<!--
  f1gp2 (F1 Grand Prix Part II / F1 Circus '92, Video System, 1992)

  ***** IMPORTANT: hiscore.dat MUST be updated for this XML to work *****
  Original hiscore.dat:
    @:maincpu,program,ff91c2,2ee,14,50
    @:maincpu,program,ffa617,3f,59,49

  PROBLEM FOUND: the full 16-GP-track + 4-point-course table needs
  768 bytes (16 x 32B + 4 x 64B), but the first range only captured
  750 bytes (0x2ee), cutting off 18 bytes short. This sliced straight
  through the middle of the very last entry (D COURSE rank 6, "CAP"),
  chopping off its 2-byte milliseconds field. The captured .hi file's
  last entry showed garbage ("9'50"5971" instead of "9'50"000") because
  hi2txt was reading those missing 2 bytes from the START of the second,
  UNRELATED memory range (ffa617) instead.

  REQUIRED FIX - extend the first range to 0x300 (768) bytes:
    @:maincpu,program,ff91c2,300,14,50
    @:maincpu,program,ffa617,3f,59,49

  This captures the complete table cleanly (all 16 GP tracks + all 4
  point ranking courses, 768 bytes) with nothing missing, and keeps the
  second (unrelated, unidentified) 63-byte range as-is afterward.
  New total file size: 768 + 63 = 831 bytes.

  Every entry was cross-checked against 8 provided screenshots of the
  actual game and matched exactly (except the corrupted last entry,
  which will resolve once hiscore.dat is updated per above).

  Byte layout confirmed:
  GP track entry (8 bytes): 3B name (ascii-offset=55) + 1B null pad
    + 1B minutes (plain int) + 1B seconds (BCD, base=16)
    + 2B milliseconds (BCD, base=16, big_endian)
  Each GP track: 3 ranked entries (24B) + 8B trailing zero pad = 32B
  16 tracks x 32B = 512B

  Point ranking course entry (8 bytes): 3B name (ascii-offset=55)
    + 1B points + 1B minutes + 1B seconds (BCD) + 2B ms (BCD, BE)
  Each course: 6 ranked entries (48B) + 16B trailing zero pad = 64B
  4 courses x 64B = 256B

  512B (tracks) + 256B (courses) = 768B total needed.
//-->
